WEBVTT

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.160
OUTSKIRTS

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:16.540
<i>Even if the light</i>
<i>Is just a little blinding</i>

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:21.450
<i>I’ll show you a word that is different</i>
<i>From all that you know</i>

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:26.160
<i>Hear my prayers, grant my desires</i>
<i>I promise I won’t be a spoiled brat</i>

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:32.950
<i>Let me be that one speck of a miracle</i>

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.500
Oh, sorry.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:54.450
OUTSKIRTS

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:06.000
RAGE

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:50.250
Account manager, have you mastered
the F chord yet?

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:56.000
Yeah... only if I have
two more of me to help out.

00:01:57.870 --> 00:01:59.290
-How's bass?
-It's stupid heavy.

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:00.830
-And drums?
-So bulky.

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:04.120
Hey, are you girls even trying?

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.830
Well...

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:09.660
I've already found an instructor
and have begun lessons.

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:11.910
-No way.
-That's amazing, Manaka!

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:17.910
Mr. Hyodo seems to be going all out too.
He ordered 5,000 more CDs for the fest.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.040
-This is serious.
-It really is do-or-die.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.200
This might be

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:26.040
our last chance to make it to the top.

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:30.370
That's why I'm giving it
everything I've got.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:34.870
My teacher laughed at me and said
it would take ten years, but I don't care.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:40.410
If Manaka's doing it, so will I.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:41.540
Me too.

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:46.160
You get it? You're on the giving end now.

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:50.700
If you can't tackle
one seemingly impossible obstacle,

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:54.790
you won't be able
to inspire anyone now, will you?

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:08.660
Sorry, are we supposed to shout something?

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:10.370
-I'm not sure.
-I think we are.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:12.120
Let's decide beforehand next time.

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:22.700
Hey.

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:24.160
Hey.

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:29.790
It's decided, then. Saturday at five.

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:32.290
Okay, I'll make sure I'm home then.

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:34.830
Great! I can't wait.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:39.500
Actually,

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:42.200
what should we do for dinner?

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:46.450
Oh, I know a real good place
near my house--

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:48.700
And that sounds lovely.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.660
But would you mind if I cooked instead?

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:55.950
Whoa! What's going on there?

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:58.330
Oh man, Inui is gunning for you hard.

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:00.200
Quit being so loud.

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:02.000
But it makes me want to scream!

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:03.700
So does this mean...

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:07.500
you're giving up on Retsuko?

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:12.750
You're cutting off your feelings for her
once and for all?

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:18.040
Inui is nice
and I really enjoy her company.

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:22.160
What's more, she might actually feel...

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:28.160
What's with the look?

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:30.750
What do you like about Retsuko, anyway?

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:34.200
You're asking me that now
when it doesn't matter anymore?

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:35.700
It does matter.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:39.580
I've been listening to your
one-sided love story for five years now.

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:41.950
At least help me understand.

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:52.700
At the office, Retsuko has a reputation

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:55.250
for being super hard-working
and kind, right?

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:57.000
Yeah.

00:04:57.370 --> 00:05:01.040
I thought she was
too hard-working, at first.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:03.700
But about half a year
after she joined the company,

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:07.330
I glimpsed her being sneaky
before she went home.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:10.500
She was acting real suspicious.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:13.500
I was curious what she was up to
and she was just...

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:19.200
She filled her bottle with water
from the office's water dispenser

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:21.700
and took it home with her!

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:23.410
Wait, what kind of story is that?

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:26.330
And it was just two 500ml bottles,
you know?

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:28.330
What are you on about?

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.160
Maybe that's when I fell for her.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:36.910
Huh? You still haven't told me
why you like her.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.750
You could say my love was built up
from simple things like that.

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:42.750
I immediately empathized with Retsuko.

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:45.620
I can also be stingy and dishonest.

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:47.700
Yeah, you are pretty dumb,
lame, and stingy.

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:49.040
That's harsh.

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:56.450
But I don't think you're dishonest.

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:01.120
I am, though.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:02.620
Even with Inui--

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:05.950
But you actually came forward
with Retsuko.

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:11.330
Hey, why are you crying?

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:13.750
I'm not crying!

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:16.870
Maybe I never had a chance
in the first place.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:20.580
I've always just been a co-worker to her.

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:23.830
Even after five years,
she still doesn't see me as a friend.

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:36.120
GOOD EVENING

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:40.370
HAIDA, DON'T YOU PLAY THE GUITAR?

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:42.000
IF YOU DON'T MIND,
CAN YOU TEACH ME?

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:43.700
Huh? It's Retsuko?

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:45.450
Why is she messaging you?

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:48.160
Not to mention, I play bass...

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:50.660
-You're turning her down, right?
-What?

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:54.040
Quit being so wishy-washy. Draw the line.

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:55.580
Um, yeah...

00:06:56.450 --> 00:06:58.790
Okay, tell me three things
you hate about Retsuko.

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:00.830
-She mistook bass for guitar.
-Good!

00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:02.410
-She never comes out drinking.
-Nice!

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:05.620
-Her mom has horrid fashion sense.
-Yes!

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:06.620
Then turn her down!

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:11.290
SURE THING.

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:13.580
SURE THING.

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:20.000
-Huh?
-Don't "huh" me, you chump!

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:28.620
SURE THING.

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:35.120
She replied again.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:37.290
Then just tell her "no" now.

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:39.540
But I already said okay.

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:42.370
You're not even trying
to cut ties with her.

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:44.580
Don't come crying to me
when the going gets tough.

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:48.330
Hm?

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:51.950
What's wrong?

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:53.910
I'M FREE ON SATURDAY.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:44.370
Oh, hey. Welcome.

00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:45.950
Were you able to find it okay?

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:48.160
Yeah, no hitches at all.

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:53.000
Sorry for springing
such a strange request on you.

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:55.250
No, it's totally fine.

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:58.250
Why do you want to play guitar
all of a sudden, anyway?

00:08:58.330 --> 00:08:59.250
Um...

00:08:59.330 --> 00:09:03.370
Well, a friend asked me
to play at her wedding...

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:05.750
I see. Sounds tough.

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:07.700
It is.

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:16.830
It made an actual sound!
And it sounded good!

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:20.750
It wasn't that great.
Besides, I don't really play the guitar.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:22.500
Wait, really?

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:25.500
I started off
on the acoustic guitar I had at home,

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:27.700
but then my friends and I started a band

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:30.450
and we needed someone on bass.

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:32.410
From then on, I always played bass.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:37.040
Oh, wow. Sorry,
I can't actually tell guitar from bass.

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:38.200
I figured.

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:42.120
Something like this?

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:44.580
Try to lay your index finger across it.

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:46.290
Like this?

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:51.160
Instead of the pad of your finger,
try using its... um, edge?

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:53.290
Do fingers even have edges?

00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:58.080
What is this?
It's impossible! My fingers hurt.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.000
-There!
-Yeah!

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:13.290
And there. And again.

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:15.290
That's it!

00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:22.080
You'll get even better if you keep at it.

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:26.540
I'll do my best, but it only gets harder
from here on, doesn't it?

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:28.500
You're finally an amateur guitarist.

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:31.500
Aw, come on,
don't put any more pressure on me!

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:33.410
But it's the truth.

00:10:34.910 --> 00:10:37.160
Thanks for today. It was fun.

00:10:37.250 --> 00:10:38.290
Yeah.

00:10:38.750 --> 00:10:41.790
Sorry, I had actually planned
to take lessons at first.

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:45.910
But I just ended up imposing on a friend.

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:50.250
Well, see you.

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:51.370
Welcome.

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:53.040
Thanks for having me.

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:55.080
I bought the ingredients.

00:11:58.910 --> 00:12:00.450
I'm borrowing some fridge space.

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:01.790
Okay.

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:04.910
I bought some pudding too,
so let's have that for dessert.

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:06.250
Thank you.

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:15.540
What's wrong?

00:12:18.700 --> 00:12:21.080
I was just thinking your place
is cleaner than I expected.

00:12:21.660 --> 00:12:23.200
I'll prepare the food now.

00:12:23.790 --> 00:12:25.910
Um, okay.

00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:42.120
You're amazing.

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:45.700
What's wrong?

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:47.620
Nothing, there's just
not enough air in here.

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:49.370
I'm sorry, though.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:52.370
Bass isn't very interesting
on its own, is it?

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:53.830
Really?

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:54.910
But I like it.

00:13:02.450 --> 00:13:03.370
Huh? What is it?

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:07.040
Something smells real good.
Oh yeah, we have curry, don't we?

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:09.750
Wow, I'm super hungry now, Inui.

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:11.830
Wanna go ahead and eat?

00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:16.830
You're right. Let's eat.

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:22.580
I'm Team Curry <i>on</i> Rice. What about you?

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:24.790
Hm... Team Curry <i>and</i> Rice.

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:27.160
You don't say? Roger that.

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:30.950
Can I use your bathroom?

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:32.330
Of course.

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:33.620
Thank you.

00:13:59.870 --> 00:14:01.410
Inui, I'm sorry.

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:04.500
I accidentally poured the curry
on top of both.

00:14:05.450 --> 00:14:06.290
Hm?

00:14:07.370 --> 00:14:08.910
Inui?

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:17.410
-I'm going home.
-What?

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:20.370
What about the curry?

00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:22.250
You can have it, Haida.

00:14:22.330 --> 00:14:25.790
Once it's cold, you can put it
in the fridge and have it tomorrow.

00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:28.830
Wait, Inui.

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:33.540
I'm sorry.

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:38.580
You haven't done anything
to warrant an apology.

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:41.040
It's fine for now.

00:14:45.830 --> 00:14:48.250
Please just tell me one thing.

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:54.700
Do you like me?

00:15:24.830 --> 00:15:27.830
Subtitle translation by Rachel Momber
